          bodyZh: `3.6 Morpheme and Word-formation
· Words and morphemes
– Words can be analyzed into morphemes.
– Morphemes are the minimal meaningful units in the composition of words.
– In word-formation, different word-forming elements are involved.
3.6.1 Affix
· Definition
– Affixes are forms that are attached to words or word elements to change or modify meaning and function.
– All affixes are bound morphemes.
– None can stand as words in their own right.
· According to function
– Inflectional affixes: -s, -ed, -ing
– Derivational affixes: pre-, ex-, de-, -less, -dom, -ic
– Derivational and inflectional affixes are identical with derivational and inflectional morphemes.
· According to distribution
– Prefixes:
◦ All derivational.
◦ Used to form new words.
◦ Examples: pre-, ex-, de-
– Suffixes:
◦ Embrace both derivational suffixes and inflectional suffixes.
◦ Examples: -less, -dom, -ic, -s, -ed, -ing
· Grouping of the above affixes
– Prefixes: pre-, ex-, de-
– Suffixes: -less, -dom, -ic, -s, -ed, -ing`,
